=base:summary.cmark

An honest, even-handed comparison of Kitchen-Sink against a few well-known
static-site generators (Hugo, Eleventy, Jekyll, Zola), and a look at what is
actually distinctive about Kitchen-Sink's own design.

=base:main-content.cmark

There is no shortage of good static-site generators. This page is not here to
declare a winner — [Hugo](https://gohugo.io/), [Eleventy](https://www.11ty.dev/),
[Jekyll](https://jekyllrb.com/), and [Zola](https://www.getzola.org/) are all
mature, well-documented tools with large communities, themes, and plugin
ecosystems that Kitchen-Sink does not try to match. What follows is a factual
side-by-side of a few structural choices, plus a plainer explanation of what
we think is actually different about Kitchen-Sink.

We have not run comparative build-time or output-size benchmarks, so this
page makes no performance claims for any of these tools.

